 34S  c  Compiled by J. Chen (NSCL, MSU), September 28, 2020                    
 34S  c  2020Ke03: E=95 MeV {+24}Mg beam was produced from the ATLAS accelerator
 34S 2c  at ANL. Target was |?200 |mg/cm{+2} {+12}C. |g rays were detected with 
 34S 3c  the GRETINA tracking array consisting of 12 modules; recoils were      
 34S 4c  separated and identified by the Fragment Mass Analyzer (FMA) with a    
 34S 5c  position-sensitive parallel-grid avalanche counter (PGAC) and an       
 34S 6c  ionization chamber. Measured E|g, I|g, |g|g-coin, particle-|g-coin.    
 34S 7c  Deduced levels, J, |p, proton-resonance energy. Discussed implications 
 34S 8c  for astrophysical {+33}Cl(p,|g) reaction rate.                         
 34S  c  All data are taken from the level scheme given in FIG.3 of 2020Ke03.   
